// Base build configuration shared by every environment.
// Environment-specific files (Debug/Staging/Release) #include this and override
// as needed. Wired to the app target via `configFiles` in project.yml.
//
// MEDIA_BASE_URL — origin for exercise media delivery (ADR-0010 §6, ADR-0011 §3/§6).
// The catalogue/manifest carry only provider-neutral RELATIVE object keys
// (`exercises/<slug>/<kind>-v<version>.<ext>`); this setting supplies the origin they
// are joined against at runtime. It is surfaced to the app through the Info.plist key
// `MediaBaseURL` (see project.yml). EMPTY BY DEFAULT — no CDN exists yet (R-02), so the
// remote media tier stays honestly inert until a real origin is configured; empty means
// "remote tier disabled" (ADR-0011 §4 tier 3).
//
// NEVER put a credential, signed URL, bucket name, or secret here (CLAUDE.md "Never
// commit"). NOTE: xcconfig treats `//` as a comment, so a real value like
// `https://cdn.example` cannot be written inline without escaping — configure a real
// origin per the deployment runbook when the backend lands, not by hand here.
MEDIA_BASE_URL =

// SYNC_BASE_URL — origin for the backend synchronisation transport (ADR-0012 §1).
// EMPTY BY DEFAULT — no backend exists yet (R-01/R-02), so the sync transport is honestly
// inert (only the DEBUG fake runs) until a real origin is configured. Surfaced to the app
// through the Info.plist key `SyncBaseURL` (see project.yml). NEVER commit a credential,
// signed URL, tenant id, or hostname here (same `//`-is-a-comment caveat as MEDIA_BASE_URL).
SYNC_BASE_URL =
